; status: works — the waterbomb base [hull2020, ch. 5]. Both diagonals and both
; center lines meet at the square's center; the 8 rays there need |M-V|=2
; (Maekawa) to be realizable. tests/test_collapse.ml empirically verified the
; contiguous 5-valley/3-mountain pattern below (corners + one edge-midpoint
; ray valley, the other three edge-midpoint rays mountain) folds to a UNIQUE
; layer order — no `over` needed.

paper square

--ac = map .b onto .d     ; diagonal a-c
--bd = map .a onto .c     ; diagonal b-d
--h  = map .a onto .d     ; horizontal midline, y = 1/2
--v  = map .a onto .b     ; vertical midline, x = 1/2

; the emitted FOLD edges_assignment is GLOBAL-frame M/V — the kernel's parity
; rule inverts face-down regions, so declared valley/mountain above differs
; from the golden letters on the four edge-midpoint rays (--h and --v).
@collapse --ac at .a and --ac at .c and --bd at .b and --bd at .d
  and --h at --(.b .c)
  and (--h at --(.a .d) mountain)
  and (--v at --(.d .c) mountain)
  and (--v at --(.a .b) mountain)
